---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../styles/service.css";

const SITE = "https://www.tmdesignengineering.com";
const url = `${SITE}/services/feasibility-study`;
const faqs = [
  ["What if you find my idea isn't feasible?", "If there's truly no way to make it work right now, then it's the best £650 you'll spend. Pressure testing and finding issues early, instead of after months of development or a tooling commitment, is the best way to approach product development. You'll still get the full report, the reasons why, and wherever possible alternative directions worth exploring, and usually there are some."],
  ["Do I need drawings or a CAD model?", "No. An idea, a description or a rough sketch is enough. If you do have designs, great, I'll factor them in, but they're not required."],
  ["Will you sign an NDA?", "Yes, happily. Protecting your idea is important, and I'm glad to work under a mutual NDA before you share anything sensitive."],
  ["What if my idea needs longer to assess?", "Some do. If that's the case, I'll tell you on the intro call and give you a fixed, scoped quote before any work starts, so you always know the price in advance."],
  ["What happens after the study?", "That's up to you. Many clients move into Concept & MVP Development or a phased product-development engagement, the study's roadmap makes scoping that straightforward. But there's no obligation: the report is yours to use however you like."],
];
const jsonld = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "@id": `${url}#service`,
    serviceType: "Product feasibility study",
    name: "Product Feasibility Study",
    description: "A fixed-price feasibility study for a new product idea: whether it can be built, the technical risks, the indicative cost and the timeline, delivered as a written report in about a week.",
    provider: { "@id": `${SITE}/#business` },
    areaServed: ["United Kingdom", "Worldwide"],
    offers: { "@type": "Offer", price: "650", priceCurrency: "GBP", url },
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Feasibility Study", item: url },
    ],
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({
      "@type": "Question",
      name: q,
      acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: a },
    })),
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="Product Feasibility Study (from £650) | Thomas McKee"
  description="A fixed-price feasibility study for your product idea, know whether it can be built, what it will cost and how long, before you spend real money. From £650."
  type="website"
  jsonld={jsonld}>
<main>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="svc-hero">
    <div class="wrap svc-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Service · Feasibility Study</span>
        <h1>Validate your product idea <em>before investing time and money in development.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">A fixed-price, fixed-scope study that analyses the technical feasibility of your idea and considers the different design directions, technologies, materials and routes to manufacture, and what their trade-offs might be. It's the technical version of commercial validation, so you can make informed decisions before diving into expensive development.</p>
        <div class="svc-hero-cta">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/#contact">Start a feasibility study <span class="arw">→</span></a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#included">Deliverables</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="spec" aria-label="Service summary">
        <div class="spec-head"><span>Service Spec</span><span>FS-01</span></div>
        <div class="spec-price"><span class="from">From</span><span class="amt">£650</span></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Deliver</div><div class="spec-v">Feasibility report</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Timeframe</div><div class="spec-v">~1 week turnaround</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">You need</div><div class="spec-v">Just an idea</div></div>
        <div class="spec-note">Standard scope studies are turned around within a week. If you want more detailed or complex analysis, like early prototypes, the service is scoped and quoted after a discovery call.</div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PAIN -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Who it's for</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">If you've asked yourself any of these</h2>
      <div class="pain">
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"Can this actually be made, or am I about to chase something impossible?"</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"What will it realistically cost and how long will it take to develop?"</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"What are the technical risks with a project like this, and how might I solve them?"</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sec-intro">A feasibility study answers all three in writing, early, while changing course is still cheap. It's usually the smartest first spend on a new product. My process is all about reducing risk and being fully informed before making important decisions. Along with a commercial viability study, this is one of the biggest long-term money savers.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT YOU GET -->
  <section class="band" id="included">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Deliverables and offerings</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">A feasibility report you can act on</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">The core deliverable is a written feasibility report: a clear document you can use to make your next decision, brief a team or take to investors. It's bookended by a discovery workshop at the start, so I properly understand what you're building, and a follow-up meeting at the end, where we go through the findings together and discuss any questions.</p>
      <div class="deliv">
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">01</div><h3>Discovery workshop</h3><p>We sit down together and work through the idea, what it has to do, who it's for and what success looks like.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">02</div><h3>Feasibility report</h3><p>The main deliverable. A written report covering everything below, honest about what will work, what might not and what it could take to manufacture.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">03</div><h3>Follow-up &amp; recommendation</h3><p>We walk through the findings together so nothing is lost in translation, and I give you a clear go / no-go / go-with-changes recommendation and a sensible next step.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sec-intro" style="margin-top:34px">The feasibility report itself covers:</p>
      <div class="scope" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
        <div class="scard">
          <ul>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> <b>Technology assessment</b>: engineering analysis, and a review of the technologies out there.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> <b>A developed project brief</b>, turning your idea and context into a clear, professional product development brief.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> <b>Routes to manufacture</b>, with indicative costs for each.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> <b>Design directions</b>, with indicative costs for each.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> <b>Material selection</b>, the best options and why.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> <b>Trade-off analysis</b>, so you can see where each decision affects the brief.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> <b>A clear recommendation</b>: a straight go / no-go / go-with-changes call, and a roadmap for the next steps.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROCESS -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">How it works</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">From idea to technically validated idea in a week</h2>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><div class="sn">1</div><div><h3>Free intro call</h3><p>You tell me the idea and we discuss whether a feasibility study is the right next step, and confirm scope and price before anything starts.</p></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="sn">2</div><div><h3>Discovery workshop</h3><p>We work through the idea together so I understand deeply what problem you're solving and what you need the study to answer. We work on the brief together.</p><div class="meta">Included</div></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="sn">3</div><div><h3>The assessment</h3><p>I dig into the engineering, the technology options, the routes to manufacture and their costs, the materials, the risks and the rough numbers, just as I would on any other project.</p></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="sn">4</div><div><h3>Report &amp; follow-up</h3><p>Everything written up as a clear feasibility report, then a follow-up meeting to walk through it, give you my recommendation and, if it makes sense, map out how to take it forward.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SCOPE -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Working together</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Clear on both sides</h2>
      <div class="scope">
        <div class="scard need">
          <h3>What you need to start</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><span class="tick">→</span> An idea or concept, a description, a sketch, or a rough model. No finished design required.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">→</span> A sense of what you want the product to do and who it's for.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">→</span> That's it! If your idea is barely more than a thought, that's exactly what this is for.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="scard">
          <h3>How I work</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> Collaborative workshops, in person or online.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> Engineering-standard reporting, curated for your product.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> Happy to work under an NDA.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> Check-ins welcome throughout.</li>
            <li><span class="tick">✓</span> A full run-through together at the end.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Before you book</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <div class="fitem"><div class="fq">What if you find my idea isn't feasible?</div><div class="fa">If there's truly no way to make it work right now, then it's the best £650 you'll spend. Pressure testing and finding issues early, instead of after months of development or a tooling commitment, is the best way to approach product development. You'll still get the full report, the reasons why, and wherever possible alternative directions worth exploring, and usually there are some.</div></div>
        <div class="fitem"><div class="fq">Do I need drawings or a CAD model?</div><div class="fa">No. An idea, a description or a rough sketch is enough. If you do have designs, great, I'll factor them in, but they're not required.</div></div>
        <div class="fitem"><div class="fq">Will you sign an NDA?</div><div class="fa">Yes, happily. Protecting your idea is important, and I'm glad to work under a mutual NDA before you share anything sensitive.</div></div>
        <div class="fitem"><div class="fq">What if my idea needs longer to assess?</div><div class="fa">Some do. If that's the case, I'll tell you on the intro call and give you a fixed, scoped quote before any work starts, so you always know the price in advance.</div></div>
        <div class="fitem"><div class="fq">What happens after the study?</div><div class="fa">That's up to you. Many clients move into <a href="/services/concept-mvp-development" style="color:var(--ember)">Concept &amp; MVP Development</a> or a phased product-development engagement, the study's roadmap makes scoping that straightforward. But there's no obligation: the report is yours to use however you like.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BRIDGE -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">What you can do with the results</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">A perfect first step in product development</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">A feasibility study stands on its own, and the report is yours to use however you like. It's a great way to be confident in raising or saving funds to develop your idea. For many founders it's also the opening phase of my <a href="/services/product-development" style="color:var(--ember)">full Product Development</a> offering, where I carry the same idea all the way through to a product that's ready to manufacture.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="band alt" id="start">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta">
        <div class="inner">
          <span class="eyebrow">Why not start now?</span>
          <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Get an answer to the idea you've been thinking about</h2>
          <p>Book a free intro call. If a feasibility study is the right next step, we'll agree the scope and price before anything begins, and about a week later you'll have your answer in writing.</p>
          <div class="row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/#contact">Book a free intro call <span class="arw">→</span></a>
            <span class="price-tag">Feasibility studies from <b>£650</b></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</Base>
